    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is five years. Collection began with the implementation of the Regulatory Compliance Rider as part of ESP IV (PUCO Case No. 22-0900-EL-SSO).&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Infrastructure Investment Rider (IIR) is a quarterly filing. Deferred R&amp;D amortization period will be determined in a future filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Storm costs are recovered over a period of twelve months. Filings are semi-annual.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period will be determined in PUCO Case No. 21-0560-EL-RDR. Timing of collection is currently unkown.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Costs for the 2020 rate case were fully amortized/written off when new base rates went into effect in November 2025 per PUCO Case No. 24-1009-EL-AIR. Amortization period for 2024 rate case costs started in November 2025 over a four year period per PUCO Case No. 24-1009-EL-AIR. Amortization period of 2025 costs is not currently known but was included in Case No. 25-0958-EL-AIR.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period is five years. Collection began with the authorization of new base distribution rates upon approval of ESP IV (PUCO Case No. 22-0900-EL-SSO) and were continued in the approval of Case No. 25-0958-EL-AIR.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The TCRR is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period will be determined in a future Rate Case or Rider as requested in PUCO Case No. 24-1009-EL-AIR. Recovery was requested in Case No. 25-0958-EL-AIR.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Economic Development Rider is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortized over twelve months beginning with the month included in rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Proactive Reliability Optimization Rider is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Distribution Investment Rider is a quarterly filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Customer Program Rider will be an annual filing. Collection has not begun yet.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Competitive bidding costs are included in the Standard Offer rates which is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The distribution portion of the TCJA is included in the annual Tax Savings Credit Rider. The transmission piece is included in the annual formula transmission rate (FERC Docket No. ER20-1068).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ACE Surge and Hypercare costs amortization began in November 2025 through base rates and will amortize over a four year period per PUCO Case No. 24-1009-EL-AIR.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Included as part of Standard Offer Rate filing which is an annual filing.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortized over twelve months beginning with the month included in rates.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Included as part of Standard Offer Rate filing which is an annual filing. The balance flipped to a regulatry asset position in 2026 and is now included on page 232.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amortization period and start date will be determined in a future order per PUCO Case No. 19-1121-EL-UNC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Proactive Reliability Optimization Rider (Vegitation Management) overcollection is refunded over a period of twelve months per PUCO Case No. 24-1009-EL-AIR. Filings are annual.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">MWH's presented are for SSO customers only. MWH for CRES customers total 3,021,887.&#160; MWH for all customers totals 3,793,395.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Unbilled MWH presented are for SSO customers only. Unbilled MWH for CRES customers totals (140,528).&#160; Unbilled MWH for all customers totals (179,918).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All revenues are for reconnect and connect fees.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Line 21 (456) Other Electric Revenues includes the following amounts: Revenues from Non-Taxable sales, Switching and Billing service revenue, and various contract and legal revenues.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Line 22 (456.1) Revenue from Transmission of Electricity of Others includes the following amounts: Transmission of Others Electricity, RTO revenues including Transmission Congestion, Losses, Firm and Non-Firm Point-to-Point, Network Integration Transmission service, Transmission Owner Scheduling, FTR Auction revenues and Expansion Cost Recovery Credits.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Revenue from Transmission of Electricity of Others includes the following amounts: Transmission of Others Electricity, RTO revenues including Transmission Congestion, Losses, Firm and Non-Firm Point-to-Point, Network Integration Transmission service, Transmission Owner Scheduling, FTR Auction revenues and Expansion Cost Recovery Credits.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Expense from Transmission of Electricity of Others includes the following: NITS, RTEP, scheduling and system control and dispatch, reactive supply and load response charges.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The annual rate used to compute amortization expense are as follows:Miscellaneous Intangible Plant: 14.29%, CIS Software- 15 year: 6.67%, SAAS Software- 5 year: 20%, SAAS Software- 3 year: 33.33%, SAAS Software- 15 year: 6.67%</link:footnote>
